          "id": "prt_msg_ses_34_02_02",
          "sessionID": "ses_34",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_34_02",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Better not to — a test that passes or fails depending on when you run it (same code, no changes) usually means there's a real bug underneath, like a race condition or an unawaited promise, not bad luck. Rerunning just hides it instead of fixing it; worth looking at what's timing-dependent in that test first."
        },
